    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d40">

                <pb facs="0151" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg55"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Bryan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-05-25"><hi rendition="#italic">May 25,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 195.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with the Department’s No. 194
                    of the 23d instant, in regard to Brazilian law, either enacted or in
                    contemplation, providing that “the importation of articles made abroad and
                    bearing labels partly or wholly in the Portuguese language, is not permitted
                    except when imported from Portugal, or when manufactured for factories,” I
                    inclose a copy of the correspondence with the Humphreys Homeopathic Medicine
                    Company in the matter.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d40-a1.xml" xpointer="d40-a1"/>
